+# PC-health / Zero-Chaos guard enforcement + Windows gate unblock — 2026-09-26
+
+## Task
+Make the existing PC-HEALTH / ZERO-CHAOS guard actually enforce the invariants the
+master goal declares, and unblock the mandatory `npm run check` gate on Windows.
+
+## Why
+The master goal makes the PC-health guard mandatory before and after every delegated
+local session and names three concrete thresholds: high CPU, available RAM below
+25%, and critically low disk must defer heavy local AI work. Auditing the existing
+implementation showed two of those signals were computed and then read by nothing,
+and a policy list that is declared as inherited was duplicated as a hardcoded regex.
+
+## Current state
+Branch `ai/master-coordinator/opencode-1790391902171-a1` at `d06cb3ed`, clean
+baseline. Three defects reproduced individually before any edit. A fourth,
+independent pre-existing failure was then found while running the required gate.
+
+## Target state
+`data/desktop-ai-policy.json` is the single source of truth for RAM floors, owned
+scratch prefixes and Desktop rules, and every one of its declared signals changes
+real behaviour. `npm run check` runs green on a Windows checkout.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `lib/agent-session-guard.js` — RAM floor enforcement, policy-driven scratch matcher, Desktop audit
+- `scripts/export-indieworlds.js` — drift comparison
+- `.gitattributes` (new) — keeps generated artifacts byte-exact
+- `test/agent-session-guard.test.js`, `test/indieworlds.test.js` — regression guards
+
+## Known risks
+- Enforcing the 25% floor (instead of only 15%) defers heavy local-model agents
+  earlier than before. This is the declared intent and matches the host-thrashing
+  incident already documented in `lib/ai-resource-scheduler.js`, but it does change
+  when local agents are allowed to start.
+- The generalized Desktop rule is restricted to *directories* so a user file such as
+  `World_server.sublime-workspace` can never block a session.
+
+## Golden systems that must be preserved
+Deny-by-default release registry, Golden UI, IndieWeb passports/RSS, the shared
+session guard for every registered agent, and the pre-existing byte-exactness intent
+of the IndieWeb export gate. No app, game, API or renderer code was touched.
+
+## Errors that must not return
+- A policy threshold that is measured, reported and then ignored.
+- A policy list duplicated as a hardcoded regex, silently ignoring `inheritForFutureAgents`.
+- Numbered/space-separated AI copy folders escaping Desktop audit.
+- A generated-artifact gate that fails on Windows purely because git rewrote LF to CRLF.
+- Turning the drift check into a false green: real content drift must still be caught.
+
+## Exact patch / change plan
+1. `snapshotResources` gains `deferHeavyWork` + reason; `preflight` throttles on it
+   instead of on the never-consumed `ramCritical` alone.
+2. `cleanupOwnedScratch` builds its matcher from `policy.ownedScratchPrefixes`
+   (regex-escaped, with the previous list as fallback).
+3. `auditDesktop` flags any Desktop *directory* whose name starts with `World_server`.
+4. `drift()` normalizes line endings and takes an optional root; `.gitattributes`
+   marks `shared/indieworlds/**` as `-text` so git stops rewriting the bytes.
+5. Focused regression tests for each defect, each proven to fail before the fix.
+
+## Tests to run
+Focused guard and IndieWeb suites; `npm run check`; `npm run check:fast`;
+`npm run desktop-ai:check`; `npm run golden:check`; `node scripts/check-agent-rules.js`;
+`npm run quality:diff`; `git diff --check`.
+
+## Deployment / PR plan
+No commit, push, PR, merge or production deployment was performed. Nothing is
+self-certified. The patch is left in the working tree for the coordinator/Architect
+to review, commit and route.
+
+## Current progress
+Implementation and focused regression tests complete. All three guard defects and
+the Windows export-gate defect are fixed and covered. Full repository suite is green.
+
+## Next action
+Architect review, then commit/push and open a PR to `master` through the existing
+coordinator flow. Requires explicit authorization — not performed by this slice.
+
+## Completion criteria
+Every regression test fails on the pre-fix code and passes after it; `npm run check`
+is green on a Windows checkout; no accepted quality metric regresses; the patch stays
+inside the existing session-guard/export subsystems.
+
+## Final evidence
+- Pre-fix reproduction, guard: 5 of 7 new tests failed (numbered-folder audit,
+  policy-driven scratch prefixes, prefix regex-escaping, enforced RAM floor, heavy
+  throttling at 25%). The 2 that passed pre-fix are deliberate guards against
+  over-correction (user-file safety, default-prefix fallback).
+- Pre-fix reproduction, IndieWeb: `checked-in static exports match canonical data`
+  and `world API remains backward-compatible` already failed on Windows, plus both
+  new drift tests failed.
+- Root cause of the export failure, proven byte-level: on-disk 43955 bytes / 742
+  CRLF vs expected 43213 bytes / 742 bare LF; content identical after CRLF→LF
+  normalization; `core.autocrlf=true`; no `.gitattributes` existed.
+- `node --test test/agent-session-guard.test.js`: 11 tests, 11 pass, 0 fail.
+- `node --test test/indieworlds.test.js`: 13 tests, 13 pass, 0 fail.
+- `npm run check`: 665 tests, 663 pass, 0 fail, 2 skipped (opt-in by design).
+- `npm run check:fast`: Syntax OK, 60 JavaScript files.
+- `npm run desktop-ai:check`: `[DESKTOP_AI_PROTOCOL] PASS`.
+- `npm run golden:check`: `GOLDEN STANDARD: PASS`.
+- `node scripts/check-agent-rules.js`: PASSED, including off-Desktop roots and
+  session-guard coverage for every registered agent.
+- `npm run indieworlds:check`: PASS — "static exports match canonical world data".
+- `git check-attr text -- shared/indieworlds/index.json`: `text: unset` (rule active).
+- `npm run quality:diff`: no accepted metric regressed; every reported metric improved.
+- `git diff --check`: clean. No UTF-8 BOM introduced.
+- Live machine check via `npm run agent-session:check`: Desktop violations 0,
+  free RAM 49.4%, free disk 177.6 GB, `deferHeavyWork=false`, roots all off-Desktop.
+- Verification of the guard's own RAM measurement: `os.freemem()`/`os.totalmem()`
+  agree exactly with `Win32_OperatingSystem.FreePhysicalMemory` (7.9 / 15.86 GB =
+  49.8%), so the guard measures the same "available RAM" the master goal specifies.
+- Files: 4 modified, 1 added, +199/-13. No app, game, API, renderer or deploy change.
+- Environment note: this worktree has no `node_modules`; suites were run with
+  `NODE_PATH` pointed at the existing canonical `node_modules` (reuse, no install).
